Summit OS wallpapers: photographs and where they come from

Summit      "Mountain" by Andy Betts, from KDE Plasma (plasma-workspace-wallpapers), CC BY-SA 4.0
Dolomites   "Canazei Granite Ridges", from the elementary OS wallpapers collection (Unsplash)
Yosemite    "Photo of Valley" and "Snow-Capped Mountain", from the elementary OS wallpapers collection (Unsplash)
Alpine Lake "A Large Body of Water Surrounded By Mountains", from the elementary OS wallpapers collection (Unsplash)
Highlands   Sean Afnan (Unsplash), from the Pop!_OS wallpapers collection
Desert      Jasper van der Meij and Jad Limcaco (Unsplash), from the Pop!_OS wallpapers collection
Dunes       "A Trail of Footprints In The Sand" (elementary OS collection) and Jared Evans (Unsplash, Pop!_OS collection)
Coast       "Odin" and "Odin (dark)", from the elementary OS wallpapers collection

Collections: https://github.com/elementary/wallpapers  https://github.com/pop-os/wallpapers
             https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-workspace-wallpapers
The pictures are cropped to 16:9. Where no night photograph of the same place exists (Dolomites, Alpine Lake,
Highlands) the dark picture is the day photograph graded to moonlight by Summit OS.
